    "field": "Antibiotic resistance in wildlife",
    "problem": "Determining the source of antibiotic resistance is challenging because it is unknown if resistance is a natural property of bacteria in wild animals or a consequence of human antibiotic use, which complicates the justification for restrictive policies.",
    "method": "We present a revised view of the thermohaline circulation that reconciles deep-ocean mixing estimates by incorporating significant wind-driven upwelling in the Southern Ocean, thereby reducing the amount of water requiring turbulent vertical mixing.",
    "task": "The task is to determine if antibiotic resistance is a natural phenomenon or a result of human activity by comparing resistance frequencies in gut bacteria from wild mammals in a low-impact area (Finland) to those in previously studied, more human-proximate populations.",
